        {
          "index": 0,
          "heading": "A typical combat encounter is a clash between two sides, a flurry of weapon swings, feints, parries, footwork, and spellcasting. The game organizes the chaos of combat into a cycle of rounds and turns. A **round** represents about 6 seconds in the game world. During a round, each participant in a battle takes a **turn**. The order of turns is determined at the beginning of a combat encounter, when everyone rolls initiative. Once everyone has taken a turn, the fight continues to the next round if neither side has defeated the other.",
          "sourceHash": "38a13e85a905018637d0a23c41d3b168d2a28ec66ba5b8f79c51671e206d5f22",
          "translationHash": "7e03df3ddac7b7fdf68e1eb8857e30d81d22e3c8152a164c9a965df5cb7ac198",
          "status": "pass"
        },
